.1(1) + R1.2(1) + R1.3(1) = 3 <= 4\n- Task 1: R1.4(1) + R1.5(1) + R2.1(1) + R2.2(1) = 4 <= 4\n- Task 2: R3.1(1) + R3.2(1) + R3.3(1) = 3 <= 4\n- Task 3: R4.1(1) + R4.2(1) + R4.3(1) = 3 <= 4\n\nAll within budget.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/dirname: core path extraction and setup (srd016-dirname R1.1-R1.3)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd016-dirname.yaml (full SRD -- focus on requirements R1.1 through R1.3)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-02.0.yaml (test cases for dirname)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel02.0-uc005-dirname.yaml (use case for dirname)\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler pattern)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (DiffTest, RunDiffTests, BuildBinary)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/dirname/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: dirname utility -- main function, flag parsing skeleton, core path extraction\n      - path: cmd/dirname/dirname_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gdirname reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd016-dirname R1.1 -- core dirname behavior that extracts the directory component from a pathname\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd016-dirname R1.2 -- handle trailing slash stripping before directory extraction\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd016-dirname R1.3 -- when path contains no slash, return dot (.)\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project SIGPIPE protocol\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use differential testing pattern -- BuildBinary(t, \\\".\\\"), exec.LookPath(\\\"gdirname\\\"), RunDiffTests\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Skip tests if gdirname is not in PATH using t.Skip\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Set LC_ALL=C in test environment per project convention\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/dirname/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/dirname/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/dirname/ -count=1 passes (skips if gdirname not found)\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"dirname /usr/bin outputs /usr\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"dirname with a path containing no slash outputs dot\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/dirname: operand handling and flags (srd016-dirname R1.4-R1.5, R2.1-R2.2)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd016-dirname.yaml (requirements R1.4, R1.5, R2.1, R2.2)\n      - cmd/dirname/main.go (existing implementation from prior task)\n      - cmd/dirname/dirname_test.go (existing differential tests from prior task)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/dirname/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: add root path handling, multi-argument support, --zero flag, end-of-options\n      - path: cmd/dirname/dirname_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: add differential test cases for R1.4, R1.5, R2.1, R2.2\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd016-dirname R1.4 -- dirname of root path (/) returns /\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd016-dirname R1.5 -- support multiple pathname operands, one output per line\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd016-dirname R2.1 -- --zero / -z flag for NUL-terminated output instead of newline\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd016-dirname R2.2 -- end-of-options marker (--) stops flag parsing\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Process each operand independently, printing one dirname result per line (or NUL-terminated with -z)\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"After --, treat all subsequent arguments as operands even if they start with a dash\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n      